<%# The row that turns a typed reference number into the submission it names.

    "PLS-845", "pls845" or the bare "845" are all somebody reaching for one
    record. sidebar_search_controller decides whether what has been typed is
    reference-shaped and points this row at SubmissionsController#lookup, which
    is what actually resolves it — nothing on this side knows which submissions
    exist or which of them the viewer may open, and a search box that guessed
    at either would be guessing about permissions.

    Rendered above the commands so Enter takes it first: somebody who typed a
    reference number wants that record, not a form whose number looks like it.

    Locals:
      row_class  the CSS class the surrounding surface styles its rows with %>
<a class="<%= row_class %>" hidden
   href="<%= submission_lookup_path %>"
   data-sidebar-search-target="reference"
   data-lookup-path="<%= submission_lookup_path %>"
   data-action="command-palette#close"
  ><span class="search-command__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>Open submission <strong data-sidebar-search-target="referenceLabel"></strong></a>
